A||||22||Homicidal||Subwoofer Placement Problem:  Bass Guys Respond PLEASE!||||8||
Z||000000||Homicidal||09-12-2000||12:45 AM||||I currently have my 10" Polk db Series sub behind my drivers seat, and I really like the sound, but the cramped space it getting hard to deal with.<P>So I wanna move it, without losing TOO much quality.  I currently have a 12 cd changer behind the passenger side seat, and I don't like the footwell idea AT ALL.<P>So what are my alternatives?  The front trunk sounds REALLY nice, but I need a PERFECT box for it.  What size dimensions do I need for the box?  Does anybody have pics?<P>I also like this idea:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/subwoof.jpg"> <P>But how do I pull it off?  What size box?<P>Any help is appreciated!<P>BTW, I found a small box at work that has the dimensions of L 20" X W 8" X H 16", would this fit in the front compartment?  It's 8" Width on the bottom and is 6" on the top, so it's a slanted box, not a perfect square.||||reg||8
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||09-12-2000||08:59 AM||||With a fiero, you're really limited space wise. There is the under the front hood box that you can go with, I was thinking someone actually produced a few of these, but I can't remeber who. Or you can replace the 4x10s with 6x9s, there's the foot well sub option, the GT counsle sub, and the behind the rear seat idea. I measured it out, and I'm willing to loose about 5 inches max behind the driver seat. Luckily, with the 'C' channel (on late '87s and most '88s I beleive) I can sink the speakers in about 2 inches. The only thing I'd worry about with that under dash mod is that the dash was not designed to with stand base vibrations, and my cause a rather annoying buzz or rattle noise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||spike||09-12-2000||10:23 AM||||I built a box for my old GT that covered the rear window. I made a plexiglass window on the front and rear of the box so I could still see behind me. I put 2 10 inch kenwood subs in the box. With this setup the subs fire at the back of your head and the passengers. The box was a little small for these 10's but I was very happy with the sound quality. It costed me about 80,00 cdn. to build the box. I am still deciding if I am going to chop my roof so I have not built another one yet for my new ride.<P>Tks. Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000003||spike||09-12-2000||10:26 AM||||Forgot to mention that I lost less then 2 inches of seat travel<P>Tks. Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||09-12-2000||11:33 AM||||i went with an 8 in the foot well but after getting my truck stereo finished (8 in each door,2-12's in back) it's not as satisfying. i had been fooling with the idea of putting two more 8's in. 1 in each door. jl audio 12 ohms. heard they were gonna stop making them so i went ahead and ordered them. hopefully if i get them (ovation is searching for 3 nationwide) and make a change to power windows, i'l be happier with my bass.<P>also looking to do something similar with my "cheap thrills" $300 fiero. looked at some cerwin vega stealth 10" free airs that i may try to get in the doors. the magnets are fairly small and the free air capability will let me vent them to make up for the lack of air space.<P>some where bettween these two ideas i wll work in a sub or subs for my indy.  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||09-12-2000||12:45 PM||||SPIKE: How did you mount the dual 10" box in the back window? would there be room for 3 10's? how muck air space did you have. CAN YOU BUILD ME ONE?!?! I have a blacked out rear window so there is no need for lexan, 1/2"-3/4" MDF would work. I plan on 3 W3 JL 10's or 2 10" Kicker Solo's How much would it cost in US$||||reg||1
